peektea is a minimal terminal file browser written in Go using Bubble
Tea. It supports vim-style navigation, previews, filtering, sorting,
hidden files, and configurable file openers.

Building requires google-go-lang (Go 1.24.4 or newer). The vendor
archive must come from the exact v0.2.1 source release and extract as
vendor/ inside the source directory. Compilation uses vendored modules
and does not download dependencies or a Go toolchain.

Optional dependencies:
  bat (https://github.com/sharkdp/bat): highlighted text previews.
  chafa (https://hpjansson.org/chafa/): image previews in the terminal.

Run "peektea init" as your normal user to configure file openers. The
configuration is stored in ~/.peektea.toml. File-opening programs must
be installed separately.
